      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Concentrations of interleukins 6 and 10, tumor necrosis factor alpha, transforming growth factor beta and C-reactive protein were measured in 42 patients before and in remote period after coronary stenting. Patients with angiographically documented in-stent restenosis compared with those without restenosis had higher initial levels of interleukin 6 and more often discontinued therapy with statins."},
